# Line-ending policy.
#
# Without this file, whether a contributor commits LF or CRLF depends on their
# personal core.autocrlf setting. That is invisible until something scans the
# bytes: cmake_lint now actually reads files, and fails a CRLF one with C0327.
# The CRLF that once reached cmake/generate_fmu.cmake was missed for exactly
# this reason -- the author had core.autocrlf=input, so it normalised on the
# way in and CI never saw it.
#
# text=auto stores every file Git detects as text with LF in the repository,
# and leaves the working-tree ending to each platform. Checkouts are unchanged
# on Windows; only the committed bytes are made consistent.
* text=auto

# Scripts executed on Linux CI runners must keep LF regardless of platform: a
# CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally named
# "/bin/bash\r", and the resulting error names neither the file nor the cause.
*.sh              text eol=lf
.run-clang-format text eol=lf
.run-cmake-format text eol=lf

# Renode scripts and platform descriptions are read by Renode on Linux.
*.resc text eol=lf
*.repl text eol=lf

# Binary -- never substitute line endings, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.fmu binary
*.zip binary
